keywords:
  - union-closed sets conjecture
  - Frankl's conjecture
  - entropy method
  - interval arithmetic
  - satisfiability
abstract: >-
  We prove that every finite union-closed family with a nonempty member has an
  element lying in at least a fraction 0.38288525996... of its members. The
  constant is the exact limit of the entropy method in the form of Liu and
  Jiang. With Jiang's global coupling the bound is strict for every family.
  We also prove the conjecture for every family of at most 52 members.
